{"ref":"BDB, כַּרְמִי","hw":"כַּרְמִי","html":"† I. <big><span dir=\"rtl\">כַּרְמִי</span></big>  <strong>n.pr.m. </strong><br><strong>1.</strong>  a son of Reuben <a data-ref=\"Genesis 46:9\" href=\"/Genesis.46.9\">Gn 46:9</a> <a data-ref=\"Exodus 6:14\" href=\"/Exodus.6.14\">Ex 6:14</a> <a data-ref=\"Numbers 26:6\" href=\"/Numbers.26.6\">Nu 26:6</a> <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 5:3\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.5.3\">1 Ch 5:3</a>.<br><strong>2.</strong>  a Judaite <a data-ref=\"Joshua 7:1\" href=\"/Joshua.7.1\">Jos 7:1</a>, <a data-ref=\"Joshua 7:18\" href=\"/Joshua.7.18\">18</a> <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 2:7\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.2.7\">1 Ch 2:7</a>; so <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 4:1\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.4.1\">4:1</a>, but read perhaps <span dir=\"rtl\">כְּלֻבַי</span> We (cf. <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 2:9\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.2.9\">2:9</a>)—𝔊 throughout χαρμ(ε)ι.","next":"BDB, כַּרְמִי²","prev":"BDB, כָּרַם"}